{
  "_comment": "Every font family a theme may name: its files under <venv>/share/fonts/<folder>/ by weight ('400i' is italic), its licence, its CSS generic family (the fallback a page names last), the system fonts a page falls back to when Google Fonts does not answer, in order (`fallbacks`, keys of LOCALS in tools/webfonts.py, measured into fallbacks.json), its `scale` when it is set larger than its nominal size (a face with a small x-height, so its text reads as large as the others': size-adjust in a PDF, font-size-adjust on a page), and where setup.py downloads it from -- a pinned release `url`, from which only files matching `take` are copied, or a pinned `raw` folder each named file is fetched from. Only OFL-1.1 families whose licence reserves no name and whose files claim no trademark belong here: free to use, embed, cut down and share under their own names, commercially too. The selftest reads each file to hold that.",

  "Geist": {
    "folder": "geist", "licence": "OFL-1.1", "generic": "sans-serif",
    "fallbacks": ["Segoe UI", "Arial"],
    "url": "https://github.com/vercel/geist-font/releases/download/v1.7.2/geist-font-v1.7.2.zip",
    "take": "^Geist-(Regular|Medium|SemiBold|Bold|Italic)\\.otf$",
    "files": { "400": "Geist-Regular.otf", "500": "Geist-Medium.otf", "600": "Geist-SemiBold.otf",
               "700": "Geist-Bold.otf", "400i": "Geist-Italic.otf" }
  },
